export const WHATSAPP_KNOWLEDGE = "## Are airport fees included?\nYes where they apply — they are part of your fixed fare, not optional extras. Dublin Airport pickup/parking (£5) is included on airport pickups together with M1 tolls where they apply; Dublin Airport drop-off fee is £0 (M1 tolls still apply). City of Derry Airport pickup (£2.50) and drop-off (£1) are included where they apply. Belfast International and Belfast City include Express Pickup or Express Drop-Off and the applicable access charge in the fixed fare. You only see the inclusions that match your direction of travel.\n\n## How much airport waiting time is included?\nAirport pickups include up to 60 minutes complimentary waiting time, giving you time to clear passport control, collect your luggage and make your way to the agreed pickup point. Pickups from non-airport locations include up to 10 minutes complimentary waiting time from the agreed pickup time. Waiting beyond the complimentary period may be charged.\n\n## Do you monitor flights?\nWhere a valid flight number has been provided, we monitor your flight and make reasonable efforts to adjust the collection time for an early or delayed arrival. Airport pickups include up to 60 minutes complimentary waiting from the actual landing time. If a significant delay means we cannot provide your booked transfer, we cancel that journey and refund in full the amount paid for it. This will not be treated as a customer cancellation or no-show.\n\n## Is meet & greet available?\nMeet & Greet with a name board and luggage assistance is included with Business Class airport pickups. For eligible Belfast International, Belfast City and Dublin airport collections, you can add optional Meet & Greet after your contact details at the price shown. Share your flight number so we can plan the collection.\n\n## How many passengers can I book for?\nCars carry up to 4 passengers. A 7 Seater Minibus carries up to 7 when available. Enter your passenger and suitcase numbers; the quote recommends a vehicle and shows the options available for your booking.\n\n## Are tolls included?\nApplicable road tolls are only mentioned when they form part of your quoted fare. Dublin Airport journeys include the M1 toll allowance on both pickup and drop-off legs. Ordinary Northern Ireland address-to-address journeys do not add separate toll charges.\n\n## Can I book a return journey?\nYes — choose Return on the quote form. Where an instant online price is shown, a 5% discount applies to the combined fare. Each leg shows its own inclusions (for example drop-off fee outbound and pickup fee plus airport waiting on the return).\n\n## How do I pay?\nGet your fixed price online. Eligible Saloon and Estate bookings can be confirmed securely by card via SumUp. On some website instant quotes you may also be offered Deposit + Cash: pay a card deposit to confirm, then pay the remaining balance in cash to your driver on the day. Card payment is not available for the remaining balance. Short-notice pickups may need Owner availability confirmation before payment. Bank transfer can be arranged where agreed.\n\n## Can I cancel my booking?\nCancel at least 24 hours before your scheduled pickup for a 100% refund of the amount actually paid. Cancellations less than 24 hours before pickup are non-refundable. A no-show after the complimentary waiting period and reasonable contact attempts is also non-refundable. If My Airport Taxi NI cancels a confirmed booking and cannot provide the journey, you will receive a full refund. If a significant flight delay means we cannot provide your booked transfer, we cancel that journey and refund in full the amount paid for it. This will not be treated as a customer cancellation or no-show. These terms do not affect any rights you have that cannot legally be excluded. This booking is for passenger transport on a specific date and time. The statutory cooling-off right that applies to some other distance contracts does not apply to this booking. Full details are in our Cancellation Policy and Terms & Conditions.\n\n## Can I change the date or time of my booking?\nMore than 24 hours before pickup you can request one free date/time change (same pickup and destination), subject to availability, via Manage Your Booking. Within 24 hours, changes cannot be made automatically — contact us on WhatsApp and we’ll do our best to help. Changing a booking does not avoid the cancellation policy. Saved quotes are not bookings: changing the date on a saved quote recalculates the fare.\n\n## What is included in the price?\nYour fixed price depends on the journey. Airport pickups: 60 minutes complimentary waiting, plus Dublin Airport pickup/parking (£5) and M1 tolls where they apply, or City of Derry Airport pickup (£2.50) where charged. Airport drop-offs: City of Derry Airport drop-off (£1) where charged; Dublin Airport drop-off fee is £0 (M1 tolls still apply). Belfast International and Belfast City include Express Pickup or Express Drop-Off and the applicable access charge in the fixed fare. Address-to-address: fixed price for your journey with 10 minutes complimentary waiting at non-airport pickups.\n\n## Do you cover City of Derry Airport?\nYes. City of Derry Airport (LDY) transfers are between LDY and the greater Belfast area (for example Belfast, Bangor, Lisburn and surrounds). Select City of Derry Airport in the quote tool — pickup (£2.50) or drop-off (£1) is included in your fixed fare where it applies.\n\n## Do you cover journeys in the Republic of Ireland?\nYes. Confirmed Greater Belfast pickups can receive instant fixed quotes to addresses throughout Northern Ireland and the Republic of Ireland. Existing eligible airport routes keep their online quotes. Other out-of-area pickups use a tailored fixed-quote request where required.\n\n## Do you provide child seats or booster seats?\nChild seats and boosters can be requested when you book, but availability is not guaranteed. Ask in advance so we can check. If a legally required child seat cannot be provided, we may be unable to carry the journey.\n\n## Can I track my driver on the day of travel?\nOn travel day we email you when your driver is on the way. Your driver may share their live location with you via WhatsApp when appropriate. We do not use a website live-tracking page.\n\n## What currency are prices quoted in?\nAll prices on this website are quoted in pounds sterling (GBP), including cross-border journeys unless we agree otherwise in writing before you travel.\n\n## Terms — Introduction\nWelcome to My Airport Taxi NI. By requesting a quotation, making a booking or using our services, you agree to these Terms & Conditions.\n\n## Terms — Operator & contact details\nMy Airport Taxi NI is a fully licensed and insured private hire operator providing pre-booked airport transfers and chauffeur services in Northern Ireland. Trading name: My Airport Taxi NI Email: bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk Telephone: 07549 815538 Website: www.myairporttaxini.co.uk Service area: Greater Belfast and across Northern Ireland Business address: Available on request (email bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk) Complaints & legal enquiries: bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk My Airport Taxi NI operates as a sole trader. Our business address is not published on this website for privacy reasons but will be provided promptly on request for legal, corporate, or booking enquiries. Please contact us if you require written confirmation of our operator status.\n\n## Terms — Our Service\nMy Airport Taxi NI provides pre-booked private airport transfers throughout Greater Belfast and surrounding areas, including transfers to and from: Belfast International Airport Belfast City Airport Dublin Airport City of Derry Airport We also provide pre-booked long-distance private transfers from Greater Belfast to destinations throughout Northern Ireland and the Republic of Ireland. Standard pickups are from anywhere within Greater Belfast. Pre-booked airport pickups are also available from Belfast International Airport, Belfast City Airport, City of Derry Airport and Dublin Airport. Pickups from elsewhere in Northern Ireland to a Greater Belfast destination receive a live online quote where route pricing is available. Other out-of-area pickups (for example outside Northern Ireland, or NI pickups to destinations outside Greater Belfast) require manual approval, do not receive an automatic online price, and cannot be paid for immediately online until we confirm a fixed quote. All journeys are subject to vehicle availability. Saloon and Estate or similar larger vehicle carry up to 4 passengers. Business Class carries up to 3 passengers. A 7 Seater Minibus carries up to 7 when it is offered and available. Business Class is a premium executive vehicle and can be booked and paid online when it is available.\n\n## Terms — Cross-border & Republic of Ireland journeys\nJourneys with a pickup or drop-off in the Republic of Ireland (including Dublin city, Eircode addresses, and Dublin Airport from Northern Ireland) are quoted individually where an instant online fare does not apply. Dublin Airport transfers may show a live online price where eligible. Other Republic of Ireland city destinations use Request Fixed Quote for manual confirmation before travel. All cross-border journeys are quoted and charged in pounds sterling (GBP) unless otherwise agreed in writing. Applicable tolls for the agreed route are included in an accepted fixed quote. Customers must select complete pickup and drop-off addresses from the Google Places suggestions on our quote form. Typed addresses that are not selected from suggestions are not accepted.\n\n## Terms — Vehicles & capacity\nSaloon and estate car transfers for up to 4 passengers are fulfilled by My Airport Taxi NI using our own licensed vehicles and drivers. A 7 Seater Minibus carries up to 7 passengers when it is offered and available. Business Class is a premium executive vehicle and can be booked and paid online when it is available. We remain your point of contact for booking, payment (where applicable), and customer service.\n\n## Terms — Booking\nCustomers are responsible for providing accurate information including: Pickup address Destination Complete addresses selected from Google Places suggestions (where the quote form requires this) Date Time Flight number (where applicable) Contact telephone number Number of passengers Number of suitcases Child seat requirements Incorrect or incomplete information may result in delays, additional charges, cancellation, or the booking being treated as a no-show without refund. Bookings are subject to vehicle availability and are not confirmed until we accept the booking in writing (including by email) or payment is completed where an instant online fare applies.\n\n## Terms — Quotations & Fares\nAll quotations are based on the information supplied at the time of booking. Where applicable, airport access charges and route tolls that form part of the quoted journey are included in the displayed fixed price. Tolls are not implied for every booking — they are included only where they form part of the agreed route (for example certain Dublin Airport journeys). Prices may change if: Pickup or destination changes. Additional waiting time is incurred beyond the complimentary allowance. Additional passengers or luggage are added. Extra stops are requested.\n\n## Terms — Booking & Payment\nFor Saloon, Estate or similar larger vehicle, and Business Class transfers where an instant fare is shown, you may pay online by card via SumUp at the end of the website quote. Your booking is confirmed once payment is completed. If you select Deposit + Cash, the amount charged online is a deposit towards the total fare. Your booking is confirmed once the deposit has been successfully paid. The remaining balance shown at checkout must be paid in cash to your driver on the day of travel. Card payment is not available for the remaining balance, so you must ensure that you have sufficient cash available at the time of pickup. Deposit + Cash is not available on Personal Quotes, Quick Quotes, saved quote links, short-notice payment links, Request Only payment links, or airport-to-airport specialist payment links. For out-of-area pickup requests, and Republic of Ireland city destinations that require a fixed quote, the process is: request a quote or booking, wait for us to confirm the fare and job, then pay via the SumUp payment link we email. Your booking is confirmed after payment is received. Payment may be made: By card via SumUp on the website (Saloon, Estate or similar larger vehicle, or Business Class with an instant fare), either the full fare or a deposit where Deposit + Cash is offered and selected By cash to the driver for the remaining balance on a Deposit + Cash booking By card via the SumUp payment link we email after confirming your booking By cash to the driver (where otherwise agreed) By bank transfer (where agreed) By any other accepted payment method we confirm in writing Payment must be made before or at the start of the journey unless a credit account has been agreed. A booking request alone does not confirm the journey.\n\n## Terms — Waiting Time\nAirport Collections Airport pickups include up to 60 minutes complimentary waiting time from the actual flight landing time. This is not unlimited waiting. Additional waiting time beyond the complimentary period may be charged. All Other Collections Pickups from non-airport locations include up to 10 minutes complimentary waiting time from the agreed pickup time. Waiting beyond this period may incur additional charges.\n\n## Terms — Significant flight delays\nWhere a valid flight number has been provided, we will monitor your flight and make reasonable efforts to accommodate a revised arrival time. If your flight is significantly delayed and, because of the revised arrival time, we are ultimately unable to provide your booked transfer, we will cancel that journey and refund in full any amount you have paid for it. This will not be treated as a customer cancellation or no-show. Flight monitoring does not guarantee that we can accommodate every delay, and our complimentary waiting period is not unlimited. Airport pickups include up to 60 minutes complimentary waiting time from the actual flight landing time. If no flight number is supplied, we cannot guarantee delayed collection without additional charges.\n\n## Terms — Cancellations & Refunds\nThe same cancellation policy applies to airport, long-distance and cross-border transfers. These terms do not affect any rights you have that cannot legally be excluded. This booking is for passenger transport on a specific date and time. The statutory cooling-off right that applies to some other distance contracts does not apply to this booking. At least 24 hours before pickup If we receive your cancellation at least 24 hours before the scheduled pickup time, we will issue a 100% refund of the amount actually paid. Less than 24 hours before pickup If we receive your cancellation less than 24 hours before the scheduled pickup time, the booking is non-refundable. Deposit + Cash bookings If you select Deposit + Cash, the amount charged online is a deposit towards the total fare. Your booking is confirmed once the deposit has been successfully paid. The remaining balance shown at checkout must be paid in cash to your driver on the day of travel. Card payment is not available for the remaining balance, so you must ensure that you have sufficient cash available at the time of pickup. Deposit + Cash is offered on eligible website instant quotes only. The remaining cash balance is due to the driver at pickup and cannot be paid by card. If you cancel at least 24 hours before pickup, we refund 100% of the amount actually paid — the card deposit. The unpaid cash balance is not charged. If you cancel less than 24 hours before pickup, the card deposit is non-refundable. The unpaid cash balance is not charged. A no-show is non-refundable in the same way. The unpaid cash balance is not charged. Significant flight delays Where a valid flight number has been provided, we will monitor your flight and make reasonable efforts to accommodate a revised arrival time. If your flight is significantly delayed and, because of the revised arrival time, we are ultimately unable to provide your booked transfer, we will cancel that journey and refund in full any amount you have paid for it. This will not be treated as a customer cancellation or no-show. Flight monitoring does not guarantee that we can accommodate every delay, and our complimentary waiting period is not unlimited. Cancellations by us If My Airport Taxi NI cancels a confirmed booking and cannot provide the journey, you will receive a full refund.\n\n## Terms — Changes to Your Booking\nYou may request one online change to your booking when more than 24 hours’ notice is provided, subject to availability. Requests made within 24 hours of the scheduled pickup cannot be amended automatically and must be agreed directly with My Airport Taxi NI. We will always try to accommodate reasonable changes, but availability cannot be guaranteed. Changing a booking does not provide a way to avoid the applicable cancellation policy. Online amendments are always recalculated using current authoritative pricing. Changing the journey details (for example addresses, passengers, luggage, vehicle, or return) may change the fare. If the new fare is higher, the additional amount must be paid before the change is confirmed. If the new fare is lower, any refund due is processed by My Airport Taxi NI. Where a change materially alters the journey, including pickup, destination, passengers or luggage, the fare is recalculated the same way. A saved quote is not a booking. If you change the date or time on a saved quote before paying, the fare is recalculated using current pricing and the original locked quote price no longer applies.\n\n## Terms — No-Shows\nA booking may be treated as a no-show where: The passenger has not attended the agreed pickup point by the end of the applicable complimentary waiting period described in Section 9; and We have made reasonable attempts to contact the passenger without success. A customer leaving the airport or another pickup location without contacting us may also be treated as a no-show where this prevents the journey from being provided. Incorrect booking information will only result in a booking being treated as a no-show where it prevents us from providing the journey after reasonable attempts to contact the customer. A no-show is non-refundable.\n\n## Terms — Child Seats\nBooster seats and child seats can be requested during booking, but availability is not guaranteed. Customers must request child or booster seats in advance so we can check what we can provide. If a legally required child seat cannot be provided, we may be unable to carry the journey.\n\n## Terms — Passenger Responsibilities\nPassengers must: Wear seat belts where required by law. Treat the vehicle respectfully. Avoid behaviour that endangers the driver or other passengers. Not smoke or vape in the vehicle. Not consume illegal drugs.\n\n## Terms — Vehicle Cleaning and Damage\nThe person making the booking is responsible for the conduct of passengers travelling under the booking. Passengers must not damage, contaminate or excessively soil the vehicle. Where a passenger causes cleaning beyond ordinary routine cleaning — including for example vomiting or bodily fluids, significant food or drink spillages, stains, pet soiling or contamination, smoking or vaping contamination, excessive mess, or deliberate or negligent damage — My Airport Taxi NI may recover the reasonable costs directly resulting from the incident. Those costs may include reasonable specialist cleaning or valeting, reasonable repair or replacement for damage, and reasonable and evidenced loss of use or driver earnings where the vehicle genuinely has to be taken out of service. Charges must be proportionate and based on reasonable loss or cost, not arbitrary penalties. Where reasonably practicable we retain evidence such as timestamped photographs, cleaning or repair invoices or receipts, the date and time the vehicle was out of service, and the associated booking or journey reference. We do not silently charge a customer’s card for these later amounts unless the payment provider and the customer’s specific payment authorisation lawfully support that exact charge. The default workflow is to record the incident, document a reasonable amount, and send an invoice or payment request with an explanation and evidence.\n\n## Terms — Luggage\nLuggage capacity depends on passenger numbers, luggage quantity and the vehicle arranged. Customers must provide accurate luggage details when booking or requesting a quote so that a suitable vehicle can be arranged. Customers must ensure: All luggage is declared during booking. Oversized luggage is advised in advance. We reserve the right to refuse luggage that cannot safely be accommodated for your passenger count (which may require a different vehicle or change the fare). Saloon and Estate are booked for up to 4 passengers; Business Class for up to 3 passengers. A 7 Seater Minibus is booked for up to 7 when it is offered.\n\n## Terms — Lost Property\nItems left in the vehicle will be retained where possible. Reasonable collection or delivery charges may apply. We cannot guarantee recovery of lost property.\n\n## Terms — Liability\nWhilst every effort is made to arrive on time, My Airport Taxi NI cannot accept liability for delays caused by circumstances outside our reasonable control, including: Traffic congestion Road closures Severe weather Accidents Police incidents Airport disruption\n\n## Terms — Complaints\nIf you are dissatisfied with our service, please contact us as soon as possible. We aim to investigate and respond to complaints promptly and fairly.\n\n## Terms — Privacy\nPersonal information is processed in accordance with our Privacy Policy at myairporttaxini.co.uk/privacy/.\n\n## Terms — Website\nWhilst every effort is made to ensure information on this website is accurate, quotations and availability are subject to confirmation.\n\n## Terms — Governing Law\nThese Terms & Conditions are governed by the laws of Northern Ireland.\n\n## Privacy — Quote and booking attempts\nWhen you receive a quote and continue towards booking, we record a random quote reference, journey, vehicle, displayed fare, timestamps and stages reached (booking started, contact stage, details submitted, payment opened and confirmed payment). This helps us operate the booking service and understand incomplete bookings. Before you submit contact details, the reference does not identify you by name, email or phone. Clicking Book My Transfer sends an immediate internal email to our team with the journey and displayed quote, even if you have not supplied contact details. Repeated clicks for the same quote are deduplicated. We do not capture what you type into contact fields for this stage tracking, subscribe you to marketing, or send customer follow-up messages from these events. Operational quote and stage records expire after 60 days. Operational emails are subject to our normal email retention practices.\n\n## Privacy — Who we are\nMy Airport Taxi NI provides pre-booked private airport transfers in Greater Belfast and across Northern Ireland. Contact: bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk · 07549 815538 Fully licensed and insured private hire operator. Business address available on request — email bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk for legal, corporate, or booking enquiries.\n\n## Privacy — Information we collect\nWhen you request a quote or make a booking, we may collect: Name, email address and mobile number Pickup and drop-off addresses (including addresses you select via Google Places on our quote form) Travel date, time and flight numbers (for airport journeys) Passenger and luggage details Saved journey details, original quoted fare and, for email saving, your email address when you choose Save My Quote Payment confirmation details from SumUp (amount, transaction reference) Optional live location if a customer chooses to share it via WhatsApp Driver GPS location history may be recorded during booked journeys for operational/dispute evidence Marketing preferences if you opt in to receive updates (optional) Limited technical signals for security, fraud prevention and advertising abuse monitoring (such as hashed network identifiers, coarse browser/device category, landing page, referrer host, and advertising campaign parameters when present)\n\n## Privacy — How we use your information\nWe use your information to: Provide quotations and confirm bookings Save journey details you request and provide a secure link by email or customer-initiated WhatsApp sharing Process card payments via SumUp Send booking confirmations and invoices by email Contact you about your journey (including SMS/WhatsApp where agreed) Send Driver on the way and arrival updates by email when applicable Record journey status and GPS route points as operational evidence for service delivery, safety and payment disputes Log bookings in our business calendar Respond to enquiries and complaints Send occasional marketing emails if you have opted in (offers, travel tips and service news) Monitor for security, fraud prevention and advertising abuse (for example repetitive paid-advertising clicks with no genuine booking activity)\n\n## Privacy — Saved quotes\nIf you use Save My Quote, we retain your journey and original price snapshot until its stated expiry, up to seven days. Email saving also requires your email address. The secure link restores your journey; the fare is recalculated before booking and may change. Saving does not create a booking. We send only the email you request. We do not send saved-quote follow-up messages or subscribe you to marketing. For WhatsApp, you choose the recipient and send the message yourself; their access to the secure link allows them to see the journey. Mobile numbers are not collected when saving. Limited hashed network and email identifiers are retained for up to one hour to restrict abuse. Keep your secure quote link private.\n\n## Privacy — Marketing emails\nWe only send marketing emails if you tick the optional marketing checkbox when booking or enquiring. This is separate from the terms you must accept to complete a booking. Marketing emails may include special offers, travel tips and news about our airport transfer and day trip services. You can withdraw consent at any time using our unsubscribe page or by emailing bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk with the address you wish to remove. We do not sell your email address to third parties for their marketing.\n\n## Privacy — Legal basis\nWe process personal data to perform our contract with you (your booking), for legitimate business interests (operating our service safely and efficiently), and where required to comply with law. Marketing emails are sent only with your consent. You may withdraw consent at any time without affecting your booking.\n\n## Privacy — Who we share data with\nWe may share limited data with trusted service providers, including: SumUp — card payment processing Cloudflare — website hosting and booking API Email delivery providers — sending confirmations Google — address autocomplete (Google Places), maps, directions, and calendar logging where configured Flight data providers — verifying flight numbers you enter Meta Platforms, Inc. / WhatsApp — when you contact us or send booking messages via WhatsApp, message content and related contact details may be processed through Meta’s WhatsApp Business Platform and our WhatsApp Business provider When our automated booking or messaging systems are connected to WhatsApp, booking and message information may be processed through Meta’s WhatsApp Business Platform and whichever WhatsApp Business provider we use. We do not sell your personal data.\n\n## Privacy — Google Places address search\nWhen you type a pickup or drop-off address on our quote form, your search text is sent to Google Places so we can show address suggestions. If you select a suggestion, Google also returns place details (such as the formatted address and place identifier) that we use to quote and book your journey. Google processes those address searches under Google’s privacy policy. We only accept addresses you select from Google’s suggestions — free-typed text alone is not used as a confirmed booking address. When you book a cross-border or Republic of Ireland transfer, we process the selected place details to quote and fulfil your journey.\n\n## Privacy — Driver tracking & location records\nWhen your driver starts tracking for a booked journey, we may record timestamped GPS points (latitude, longitude, accuracy, speed and heading where the device provides them). We use this data to show you a live tracking page, to operate the journey safely, and to keep an internal journey record that may support payment or service disputes. A journey record does not guarantee the outcome of any card chargeback. Journey and driver location information, together with booking-event information, may be recorded and retained where necessary for providing and managing the booked service, safety and security, resolving complaints, fraud prevention, payment and refund disputes, and establishing or defending legal claims. We email Driver on the way and arrival updates on travel day. Your driver may share live location via WhatsApp when appropriate. We do not use a public website live-tracking page. We do not intentionally collect unnecessary device identifiers beyond what is needed to operate location sharing, and we do not add invasive device fingerprinting solely for chargeback purposes.\n\n## Privacy — Retention\nBooking and payment records are kept as long as needed for customer service, accounting, tax and dispute resolution — typically up to 6 years where required for tax or accounting, then deleted or anonymised where we no longer need them. Saved quotes are kept for the 7-day validity window and a short additional period for audit and conversion tracking, then removed automatically from active storage. Driver GPS journey evidence is retained as an operational/dispute record for a configurable period (default around 13 months / ~400 days unless a longer period is set for the business). It is not retained indefinitely. Journey records and any operational GPS evidence are retained only as needed for disputes, safety, and legal requirements. Optional WhatsApp live location is controlled by the sender inside WhatsApp. Refund and cancellation audit records are kept with the related booking for the same accounting/dispute retention period. Advertising abuse / security monitoring event records are retained for about 90 days, then removed or anonymised. Aggregated non-identifying statistics may be kept longer.\n\n## Privacy — Your rights\nUnder UK GDPR you may request access, correction or deletion of your personal data, or object to certain processing. Contact us at bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk. You may also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO).\n\n## Privacy — Cookies\nThis website uses essential browser storage to remember payment return state during checkout and to store your cookie preference. We may also use a short-lived essential session identifier for security, fraud prevention and advertising abuse monitoring. This is separate from optional marketing measurement and is not used to identify individual competitors. Optional Google Ads cookies are used only if you choose “Accept measurement cookies” on our consent banner. When accepted, we load the Google tag sitewide with Google Consent Mode so Google may measure fixed-price quotes, saved booking requests and completed paid bookings, subject to that consent choice. The Google tag may set Google cookies used for conversion measurement. It is not used for general site analytics browsing tracking. With your consent, we may also send securely hashed booking contact details (such as email or phone) to Google as enhanced conversions to improve measurement accuracy. These details are hashed in the browser before they are sent. You can change your mind later by clearing site data for this website in your browser settings; the consent banner will appear again if no preference is stored.\n\n## Privacy — Changes\nWe may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when it was last revised.\n\n## Live flight monitoring\nWhere a valid flight number has been provided, we monitor your flight and make reasonable efforts to adjust the collection time. Airport pickups include 60 minutes complimentary waiting from the actual landing time.\n\n## A driver reserved for your journey\nYour confirmed transfer has a driver and pickup time allocated in advance, with travel-day updates provided where applicable. On travel day we email you when your driver is on the way, and they may share their live location via WhatsApp when appropriate.\n\n## Business Class Meet & Greet\nBusiness Class airport pickups include Meet & Greet in arrivals with a name board and luggage assistance. Saloon, Estate and 7 Seater pickups use the agreed airport pickup point. Share your flight number when you book.\n\n## 60 minutes airport waiting\nAirport pickups include up to 60 minutes complimentary waiting time, giving you time to clear passport control, collect your luggage and make your way to the agreed pickup point.\n\n## Clear fixed quotes\nSee only the inclusions that apply to your journey — express airport fees where relevant, Dublin tolls where they apply, and simple fixed prices for address-to-address trips.\n\n## Book online 24/7\nRequest a transfer online any time — including early mornings, late nights, bank holidays and Christmas. Bookings are confirmed in advance for your chosen pickup time.\n\n## Cars and 7-seater airport transfers\nChoose Saloon, Estate, Business Class or a 7 Seater Minibus when available. Saloon and Estate carry up to 4 passengers, Business Class up to 3 and the minibus up to 7; enter your luggage for a suitable vehicle recommendation and a fixed quote.\n\n## Airports we cover\nWe cover Belfast International (BFS): Direct transfers to and from Aldergrove with live flight monitoring and complimentary waiting time. Get a fixed quote, ~30 min from Belfast George Best Belfast City (BHD): Quick, convenient transfers to the heart of Belfast — ideal for business and short-haul flights. Get a fixed quote, ~15 min from city centre Dublin Airport (DUB): Comfortable cross-border transfers between Belfast and Dublin Airport, with fixed quotes and applicable M1 tolls included. Get a fixed quote, ~2 hrs from Belfast City of Derry (LDY): Transfers between City of Derry Airport and the greater Belfast area — departures from Bangor, Belfast, Lisburn and surrounds, or airport collections at LDY arrivals heading east. Get a fixed quote, Belfast area ↔ Derry Airport Airport pickups include the applicable airport pickup fee (Dublin Airport pickup/parking £5 plus M1 tolls, or City of Derry Airport pickup £2.50) and 60 minutes complimentary waiting after landing. Airport drop-offs include the applicable airport drop-off fee where charged (City of Derry Airport £1; Dublin Airport drop-off fee £0 with M1 tolls). Belfast International and Belfast City include Express Pickup or Express Drop-Off and the applicable airport access charge in the fixed fare. Address-to-address journeys are a fixed price for your route.\n\n## Areas we cover\nWe cover towns and areas across Northern Ireland including Belfast City Centre, Lisburn, Bangor, Newtownabbey, Holywood, Carrickfergus, Antrim, Ballyclare, Ballymena, Coleraine, Derry / Londonderry, Newry, Armagh, Portadown, Lurgan, Downpatrick, Newcastle, Larne, Banbridge, Enniskillen, Omagh, Cookstown, Newtownards, Comber, Dundonald, Hillsborough, Carryduff, Moira, Glengormley, Whiteabbey.\n\n## Fleet and vehicles\nEstate Car (1–4 passengers): 1–4 passengers — spacious estate with a large boot for family holidays and airport luggage. Instant online price. Standard Saloon (1–4 passengers): 1–4 passengers — ideal for solo travellers and couples with light luggage. Instant online price. Business Class (1–4 passengers): Premium executive vehicle. Book and pay online when Business Class is available.\n\n## Vehicle booking guidance\n1–4 passengers: Saloon or Estate instant quote where eligible. Pay online by card to confirm. Cars carry up to 4 passengers; the 7 Seater Minibus carries up to 7 when enabled and available.\n\n## Passenger capacity\nMy Airport Taxi NI provides private airport transfers. Online quotes offer Saloon and Estate or similar larger vehicle for 1–4 passengers, and Business Class for 1–3 passengers, and a 7 Seater Minibus when it is offered and the party fits. All enabled vehicle categories stay visible. A vehicle that cannot take the passengers and luggage is shown but cannot be selected. Enter your passengers and luggage for a suitable recommendation.\n\n## Operator and business details\nMy Airport Taxi NI — Fully licensed and insured private hire operator. Service area: Greater Belfast and across Northern Ireland. Jurisdiction: Northern Ireland, United Kingdom. Email bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk, telephone 07549 815538. Business address available on request — email bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk for legal, corporate, or booking enquiries. Website https://www.myairporttaxini.co.uk.\n\n## Contact details\nCall 07549 815538, WhatsApp @belfasttaxi, email bookings@myairporttaxini.co.uk, or save our contact card from this chat or https://www.myairporttaxini.co.uk/contact/.\n\n## Booster seats and child seats\nBooster seats and child seats can be requested during booking, but they are not guaranteed. Please request them in advance so we can check availability. If a legally required child seat cannot be provided, we may be unable to carry the journey.\n\n## Meet and greet\nBusiness Class airport pickups include Meet & Greet in arrivals with a name board and luggage assistance. For eligible Belfast International, Belfast City and Dublin airport collections, you can add optional Meet & Greet after your contact details at the price shown. Share your flight number so we can plan the collection.\n\n## Flight delays and waiting time\nWhere a valid flight number has been provided, we monitor the flight and make reasonable efforts to adjust the collection time. Airport pickups include up to 60 minutes complimentary waiting from the actual landing time. If a significant delay means we cannot provide the booked transfer, we cancel that journey and refund in full the amount paid for it. This will not be treated as a customer cancellation or no-show. Flight monitoring does not guarantee every delay, and complimentary waiting is not unlimited. Airport drop-offs include the applicable airport drop-off fee where charged. Non-airport pickups include 10 minutes complimentary waiting. Dublin Airport pickups include pickup/parking (£5) and M1 tolls; Dublin drop-off fee is £0 with M1 tolls still included. City of Derry Airport pickup is £2.50 and drop-off is £1.\n\n## Cash and payment options\nTransfers with an instant fare can pay by card online via SumUp at the end of the website quote. Otherwise, after you Request to book and we confirm the job, we email a SumUp payment link. Cash to the driver or bank transfer can be arranged where agreed.\n\n## Terms last updated\nOur Terms & Conditions were last updated September 2026 v2. Full details are on https://www.myairporttaxini.co.uk/terms/.\n\n## Private Long-Distance Transfers from Anywhere in Greater Belfast\nPre-booked, door-to-door private transfers from anywhere in Greater Belfast to destinations throughout Northern Ireland and the Republic of Ireland. Airport pickups are also available from Belfast International Airport, Belfast City Airport, City of Derry Airport and Dublin Airport. Standard pickups are from Greater Belfast (plus Belfast International, Belfast City, City of Derry, and Dublin Airport). Pickups from elsewhere in Northern Ireland to a Greater Belfast destination can receive a live online quote where available. Destinations can be anywhere in Northern Ireland or the Republic of Ireland. Other out-of-area pickup requests need Request Fixed Quote for manual approval — no automatic online fare or immediate payment until confirmed. Greater Belfast pickups to confirmed destinations across Ireland can receive an instant quote. Dublin Airport and other existing eligible airport routes keep their online quote and booking flow.\n\n## Long-distance — Greater Belfast pickups\nStandard pickups are from anywhere in Greater Belfast — home, hotel or business address.\n\n## Long-distance — Destinations across Ireland\nTravel to destinations throughout Northern Ireland and the Republic of Ireland. Enter any supported address on the quote form.\n\n## Long-distance — Airport pickups\nPre-booked pickups are also available from Belfast International Airport, Belfast City Airport, City of Derry Airport and Dublin Airport.\n\n## Long-distance — Fixed quotes where needed\nConfirmed Greater Belfast pickups can show instant fixed prices to addresses throughout Northern Ireland and the Republic of Ireland. Other out-of-area pickups retain their existing quote rules.\n\n## Long-distance example routes\nExample long-distance routes from Greater Belfast: Belfast city centre to Dublin Airport; Bangor to Cork city; Lisburn to Galway; Newtownabbey to Dublin city centre; Holywood to Donegal; Belfast International Airport to Dublin city.\n\n## Locations we cover\nStandard long-distance pickups are from Greater Belfast (plus Belfast International, Belfast City, City of Derry, and Dublin Airport). Destinations can be anywhere in Northern Ireland or the Republic of Ireland. Lists below are examples only — enter exact addresses on the quote form. Republic of Ireland example destinations: Dublin city centre, Dublin Airport (DUB), Cork, Galway, Limerick, Donegal, Sligo. Airports: Belfast International (BFS), George Best Belfast City (BHD), Dublin Airport (DUB), City of Derry (LDY). Example journeys from Greater Belfast pickups — not an exhaustive list, and not an offer of standalone pickups from the destination cities. Popular routes: Belfast to Dublin city; Bangor to Cork; Lisburn to Galway; Newtownabbey to Donegal.\n\n## Belfast Cruise Terminal Transfers\nMy Airport Taxi NI provides pre-booked private transfers for passengers arriving at or departing from Belfast Cruise Terminal. If you need a Belfast cruise port taxi after you leave the ship, or a morning collection from a hotel to the cruise port, we reserve a Saloon or Estate for your party rather than leaving you to find a car at the harbour. Page: https://www.myairporttaxini.co.uk/belfast-cruise-terminal-transfers/ Typical journeys: Belfast Cruise Terminal to Belfast International Airport; Belfast Cruise Terminal to Belfast City Airport; Belfast Cruise Terminal to Dublin Airport; Cruise terminal to Belfast hotels; Hotels to Belfast Cruise Terminal; Other onward destinations. Meeting point: We do not guarantee pickup immediately beside the ship. Cruise berth and pedestrian access arrangements can change with each call, so the precise meeting point is confirmed where necessary before travel. Time to an onward flight: If you are flying after you disembark, allow a generous gap between the scheduled ship arrival and check-in. Disembarkation can run later than the published time, and we cannot guarantee how quickly passengers will be cleared to leave the terminal. Vehicle and passengers: Saloon and Estate carry up to 4 passengers, subject to luggage capacity. For larger groups, enquire about a 7 Seater Minibus. Suitcases from a week at sea often decide the car before the passenger count does. How to book: Cruise-terminal collections are arranged by enquiry so we can confirm the meeting point and timing. WhatsApp or the contact page is the most reliable start. The homepage quote tool remains available for standard airport transfers once you have an address and flight time. Cruise-terminal collections are arranged by enquiry. Do not quote a cruise fare, apply airport waiting-time rules to the harbour, offer shore excursions, or claim we are an official Belfast Harbour or cruise operator.\n\n## Dublin Airport Transfers to & from Northern Ireland\nPre-book a private transfer to or from Dublin Airport (DUB), with Belfast, Bangor, Lisburn and surrounding towns in our Northern Ireland service area. Choose a departure transfer from your home or hotel to the airport, or an arrival collection from Dublin Airport to your Northern Ireland address. Tell us whether you need Terminal 1 or Terminal 2 when known. Enter your journey details for a fixed-price quote with applicable tolls included. Where a valid flight number has been provided, we monitor your flight and make reasonable efforts to adjust the collection time. Airport pickups include 60 minutes complimentary waiting from the actual landing time. Fixed prices for NI ↔ Dublin Airport journeys Applicable tolls included on Dublin Airport fares Up to 60 minutes complimentary waiting time on airport pickups Applicable airport access charges included in your fixed fare 5% return-booking discount on the combined journey fare, excluding fixed charges and surcharges Allow around two hours for the road journey from Belfast in normal traffic, plus the time your airline recommends for check-in and security. Allow extra travel time during busy periods. For early Dublin departures, overnight or very early pickups from Bangor, Belfast, and Lisburn are common. For departures, select Dublin Airport as your destination and tell us whether your flight leaves from Terminal 1 or Terminal 2 when known. For arrivals, select Dublin Airport as your pickup and provide your flight number when completing the booking. Your driver meets you in Arrivals at Terminal 1 or Terminal 2 after you collect your bags. Get your fixed price based on your journey. Around 2 hours from Belfast in normal traffic Areas often served: Belfast, Lisburn, Bangor, Newtownabbey, Carrickfergus, Ballyclare, Holywood, Antrim, Ballymena, Larne, Newry, Newtownards, Dundonald, Comber, Carryduff, Hillsborough, Moira, Glengormley, Whiteabbey, Northern Ireland, Dublin Airport.\n\n## City of Derry Airport Transfers\nCity of Derry Airport (Eglinton) connects the north-west with UK routes. We specialise in transfers between LDY and the greater Belfast area — not short local Derry city hops — so Bangor, Belfast, and Lisburn travellers can travel with one clear booked price. Belfast-area ↔ Derry Airport focus (Bangor, Belfast, Lisburn and surrounds) Flight monitoring with up to 60 minutes complimentary waiting on airport pickups Guide pricing shown online with confirmation before payment Business Class airport pickups include Meet & Greet with a name board Pickup must be in the greater Belfast area for journeys to LDY — enter a Bangor, Belfast, or Lisburn-area address in the quote tool. For arrivals at LDY heading to Belfast/Bangor, share your flight number so we can adjust for delays. For an arrival collection, select City of Derry Airport as your pickup and enter your Belfast-area destination. Follow the agreed collection instructions after collecting your luggage. These are longer inter-city runs; return bookings are popular for weekend trips. Get your fixed price based on your journey. Belfast area ↔ Derry Airport (longer inter-city transfer) Areas often served: Belfast, Bangor, Lisburn, Newtownabbey, City of Derry Airport.\n\n## Belfast International airport summary\nBelfast International (BFS): Direct transfers to and from Aldergrove with live flight monitoring and complimentary waiting time. Get a fixed quote. Typical timing: ~30 min from Belfast.\n\n## George Best Belfast City airport summary\nGeorge Best Belfast City (BHD): Quick, convenient transfers to the heart of Belfast — ideal for business and short-haul flights. Get a fixed quote. Typical timing: ~15 min from city centre.\n\n## Dublin Airport airport summary\nDublin Airport (DUB): Comfortable cross-border transfers between Belfast and Dublin Airport, with fixed quotes and applicable M1 tolls included. Get a fixed quote. Typical timing: ~2 hrs from Belfast.\n\n## City of Derry airport summary\nCity of Derry (LDY): Transfers between City of Derry Airport and the greater Belfast area — departures from Bangor, Belfast, Lisburn and surrounds, or airport collections at LDY arrivals heading east. Get a fixed quote. Typical timing: Belfast area ↔ Derry Airport.\n\n## Belfast airport transfers\nFrom city-centre hotels and business districts to south Belfast and the Titanic Quarter, we cover Belfast pickups for every major airport. Quote address hint: Belfast.\n\n## Newtownabbey airport transfers\nNewtownabbey and the Shore Road corridor are well placed for Belfast International and Belfast City Airport runs, with straightforward access to the M2. Quote address hint: Newtownabbey.\n\n## Carrickfergus airport transfers\nCarrickfergus and Greenisland sit on the A2 Shore Road — a regular pickup zone for both Belfast airports and for Dublin departures. Quote address hint: Carrickfergus.\n\n## Ballyclare airport transfers\nBallyclare sits on the A57 towards Aldergrove, so Belfast International is usually the shorter Belfast airport run from the town. Quote address hint: Ballyclare.\n\n## Lisburn airport transfers\nLisburn and surrounding BT28/BT27 areas are a regular pickup zone for Aldergrove, City Airport, and Dublin Airport transfers. Quote address hint: Lisburn.\n\n## Bangor airport transfers\nBangor and North Down are among our most requested pickup areas — especially for early Belfast International flights and Dublin Airport runs. Quote address hint: Bangor.\n\n## Holywood airport transfers\nHolywood and the Cultra–Seahill stretch of the A2 are a regular North Down collection area for all three airports. Quote address hint: Holywood.\n\n## Antrim airport transfers\nAntrim, Templepatrick and the A26 corridor are among the closest towns we collect for Belfast International Airport. Quote address hint: Antrim.\n\n## Ballymena airport transfers\nBallymena and the Galgorm–Broughshane hinterland are a core mid-Antrim collection area, especially for Belfast International. Quote address hint: Ballymena.\n\n## Larne airport transfers\nLarne, Islandmagee and the A8 corridor are collected as east-Antrim harbour jobs — not as Carrickfergus Shore Road pickups. Quote address hint: Larne.\n\n## Newry airport transfers\nNewry and the Warrenpoint–Rostrevor coast are on the A1/M1 corridor — well placed for Dublin Airport and still a regular origin for both Belfast airports. Quote address hint: Newry.\n\n## Newtownards airport transfers\nNewtownards and the A20 toward Dundonald are an Ards pickup zone for both Belfast airports and for Dublin departures. Quote address hint: Newtownards.\n\n## Dundonald airport transfers\nDundonald sits on the A20 between east Belfast and Newtownards, a regular start for City Airport and for longer International and Dublin runs. Quote address hint: Dundonald.\n\n## Comber airport transfers\nComber and the north-west corner of Strangford Lough are collected via the A22 to Dundonald, not as Newtownards or Bangor jobs. Quote address hint: Comber.\n\n## Carryduff airport transfers\nCarryduff and the Saintfield Road are a south-Belfast pickup zone for Aldergrove, City Airport and Dublin. Quote address hint: Carryduff.\n\n## Hillsborough airport transfers\nHillsborough village and the A1 bypass are quoted from the address you enter, not as a generic Lisburn job. Quote address hint: Hillsborough.\n\n## Moira airport transfers\nMoira and the M1 junction are a regular pickup for Dublin Airport and for both Belfast airports. Quote address hint: Moira.\n\n## Glengormley airport transfers\nGlengormley and Sandyknowes are the M2 start for Aldergrove, with City Airport and Dublin booked as separate routes. Quote address hint: Glengormley.\n\n## Whiteabbey airport transfers\nWhiteabbey and the A2 Shore Road are a lough-side pickup zone, separate from Glengormley and Sandyknowes. Quote address hint: Whiteabbey.\n\n## Craigavon airport transfers\nCraigavon, Portadown and Lurgan are on the M1 corridor — handy for Belfast International via Moira, Belfast City through Belfast, and Dublin Airport via the A1. Quote address hint: Craigavon.\n\n## Coleraine airport transfers\nColeraine, Portrush and Portstewart are on the Causeway Coast — the A26 runs south to Belfast International, on to Belfast City via the M2, and to Dublin Airport via the M1 and A1. Quote address hint: Coleraine.\n\n## Banbridge airport transfers\nBanbridge is on the A1 corridor — north to Belfast International and Belfast City, or south past Newry to Dublin Airport. Quote address hint: Banbridge.\n\n## Downpatrick airport transfers\nDownpatrick and the Lecale area — up the A7 to Belfast City and Belfast International, or west towards Newry for Dublin Airport. Quote address hint: Downpatrick.\n\n## Newcastle airport transfers\nNewcastle, Co Down at the foot of the Mournes — the A24 north to the Belfast airports, or the A50 and A1 south to Dublin Airport. Quote address hint: Newcastle, County Down.\n\n## Armagh airport transfers\nArmagh sits between the Belfast airports and Dublin — the A3 and M1 lead to Belfast International and Belfast City, and the A28 to Newry leads south to Dublin Airport. Quote address hint: Armagh.\n\n## Dungannon airport transfers\nDungannon is at the western end of the M1 — east to Belfast International and Belfast City, and south via Newry or Monaghan to Dublin Airport. Quote address hint: Dungannon.\n\n## Cookstown airport transfers\nCookstown and Magherafelt sit west of Lough Neagh — the A6 via Toome leads to Belfast International and Belfast City, and the A29 and M1 lead south to Dublin Airport. Quote address hint: Cookstown.\n\n## Omagh airport transfers\nOmagh and west Tyrone sit on the A5 — east over the A505 or A4 to Belfast International and Belfast City, or south via Aughnacloy and the N2 to Dublin Airport. Quote address hint: Omagh.\n\n## Enniskillen airport transfers\nEnniskillen and the Fermanagh lakelands are long transfers — the A4 east to Belfast International and Belfast City, or south through Cavan on the N3 and M3 to Dublin Airport. Quote address hint: Enniskillen.\n\n## Derry airport transfers\nDerry~Londonderry and Limavady are long transfers — the A6 over the Glenshane Pass to Belfast International and Belfast City, or the A5 and N2 south to Dublin Airport. City of Derry Airport is covered too. Quote address hint: Derry~Londonderry.\n\n## Ballycastle airport transfers\nBallycastle, Bushmills and the Glens of Antrim are on the north coast — the A44 and A26 to Belfast International, the M2 to Belfast City, and the M1 south to Dublin Airport. Quote address hint: Ballycastle.\n\n## Chauffeur and executive private hire\nWe provide chauffeur and executive private hire across Northern Ireland for business travel, events, and as-directed journeys — as well as our airport transfer service. Contact us via WhatsApp for a personalised quote.\n\n## Giant's Causeway & Causeway Coast\nExplore Northern Ireland's most iconic coastline — hexagonal basalt columns, dramatic cliffs, and Atlantic views. A private Giant's Causeway tour from Belfast in your own car with a local driver — no coach, no fixed timetable and no strangers in your group. We collect you from your Belfast hotel, home or the cruise terminal and follow the Causeway Coast to the UNESCO World Heritage stones, with stops at Carrick-a-Rede Rope Bridge, Dunluce Castle and Ballintoy Harbour along the way. Take as long as you like at each stop: the route is planned around you, and your driver knows the quieter viewpoints and the best places for lunch. Duration: Full day (~8 hours). Price: From £395. Price per car, not per person: up to 4 passengers in a Saloon or Estate, collected from your Belfast hotel, home or Belfast Cruise Terminal. Attraction entry tickets are not included. Picking up outside Belfast? We'll confirm the price when you enquire. Highlights: Giant's Causeway UNESCO World Heritage Site; Carrick-a-Rede Rope Bridge (seasonal access); Dunluce Castle clifftop ruins; Ballintoy Harbour and coastal villages; Flexible photo and refreshment stops.\n\n## Belfast City Highlights\nDoor-to-door transport to Belfast's landmarks, murals, Titanic Quarter, and the best of the city centre. See Belfast at your own pace on a private half-day city tour by car. Your driver collects you from your hotel, home or Belfast Cruise Terminal and takes you round the city's highlights — Titanic Belfast and the Titanic Quarter, City Hall, the Cathedral Quarter, the political murals and peace walls, and Stormont. Spend longer where you want and skip what you don't: history, architecture, food stops or a bit of everything. Duration: Half day (~4 hours). Price: From £195. Half day, around 4 hours. Ideal for cruise passengers, day visitors or a few hours before a flight. Price per car, not per person: up to 4 passengers in a Saloon or Estate, collected from your Belfast hotel, home or Belfast Cruise Terminal. Attraction entry tickets are not included. Picking up outside Belfast? We'll confirm the price when you enquire. Highlights: Titanic Belfast and Titanic Quarter; City Hall and Cathedral Quarter; Political murals and peace walls; Stormont Parliament Buildings; Local lunch and coffee stop recommendations.\n\n## Game of Thrones Filming Locations\nVisit iconic Westeros filming sites across County Antrim and beyond — Dark Hedges, coastal castles, and more. Northern Ireland was the backdrop for much of Game of Thrones. On this private tour from Belfast your driver takes you to the most recognisable filming locations on the Antrim coast — the Dark Hedges, Ballintoy Harbour, Cushendun Caves and more — in your own car, at your own pace. Perfect for fans who want to see several sites in one comfortable day, and easy to combine with the Giant's Causeway. Duration: Full day (~8 hours). Price: From £395. Full day, around 8 hours. Route can be tailored to your favourite locations. Price per car, not per person: up to 4 passengers in a Saloon or Estate, collected from your Belfast hotel, home or Belfast Cruise Terminal. Attraction entry tickets are not included. Picking up outside Belfast? We'll confirm the price when you enquire. Highlights: Dark Hedges avenue; Ballintoy Harbour (Iron Islands); Dunluce Castle; Cushendun Caves; Additional locations by request.\n\n## Antrim Coast Scenic Drive\nA relaxed coastal journey from Belfast to the Glens of Antrim — beaches, harbours, and sweeping sea views. The Antrim Coast Road is one of the finest scenic drives in the UK. Sit back on a private tour from Belfast through seaside villages, the Glens of Antrim and clifftop viewpoints — without the stress of narrow roads or finding parking. Choose a half day along the coast to Carnlough and Glenarm, or a full day taking in Cushendall, Glenariff Forest Park and Ballycastle. Duration: Half to full day (~5–8 hours). Price: From £195. Half day (around 4 hours) from £195, full day (around 8 hours) from £395. Price per car, not per person: up to 4 passengers in a Saloon or Estate, collected from your Belfast hotel, home or Belfast Cruise Terminal. Attraction entry tickets are not included. Picking up outside Belfast? We'll confirm the price when you enquire. Highlights: Glens of Antrim coastal route; Glenariff Forest Park (seasonal); Cushendun and Cushendall villages; Ballycastle and Rathlin Island views; Flexible lunch stops at coastal pubs.\n\n## Day trip benefits\nYour own private vehicle: Travel in comfort with a dedicated driver — no shared coaches, no fixed schedules, and no strangers in your group. We know the routes: Our drivers know the best roads, viewpoints, and lunch spots across Northern Ireland, with flexibility to adapt on the day. Door-to-door service: We collect you from your Belfast hotel, B&B, home or Belfast Cruise Terminal and bring you back when you're ready. Clear prices: Half days from £195 and full days from £395 — per car, not per person, for up to 4 passengers. We confirm your exact price before you book.";
